  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results Indicator #1: Public spending on overseas medical treatment as a percentage of GDP</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2017-06-30" value="10" year="2017"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2017-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="7">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">[Slow Progress] Expenditure on overseas medical treatment (TOMRS) spiked primarily due to post-COVID increase on health travel following border reopening. Spending on TOMRS is expected to stabilize around the baseline over the short- to medium-term. This is because overseas referrals are critical to allow Tuvaluans access to tertiary healthcare. However, there is room to generate greater cost efficiencies in the scheme. The Ministry of Health and Social Welfare is considering recommendations for improved efficiencies based on a locally-supported review of the scheme.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="13.40"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results Indicator #3: Average share of procurement (by value) executed through competitive bidding, excluding direct procurement of COVID related supplies.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2017-06-30" value="47" year="2017"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2017-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="55">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">[Achieved] In 2022, procurement was limited to COVID-related supplies. However, in 2023, only 15.8 percent of procurement (by value) was executed through competitive bidding. Despite increased project implementation following the reopening of borders, competitive bidding remained low due to market proximity challenges and limited interest from international contractors. In 2024, the MFED organized refresher workshops for government stakeholders on procurement processes and best practices. During these sessions, MFED emphasized that competitive procurement is not only a regulatory requirement but also a strategic approach to ensuring transparency, accountability, and the efficient use of resources. As a result, line ministries gained a stronger understanding of its importance, leading to 69 percent of procurement being conducted through competitive bidding since July 2024.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="69"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results Indicator #7: Quantity of recyclable waste exported.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2018-06-30" value="0 tonnes" year="2018"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="20 tonnes">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">[On Track] Tuvalu exported 14 tonnes of recyclable waste in 2024 (aluminum cans) and 30 tonnes of hazardous waste during 2020 to 2024. The Waste Management Department faces challenges in maintaining its equipment and machineries that process recyclable waste and ready it for export.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="14 tonnes"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results Indicator #2: The adult population registered and treated for hypertension and diabetes at enhanced primary health care clinics and specialized NCD outpatient clinic at the PMH</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-06-30" value="21" year="2019"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="35">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">[Achieved] The rollout of the Community-NCD health-worker initiative has made significant progress. 1,802 (90 percent of total) NCD cases have been registered for home visits, with 253 cases referred for further management (14 percent of total) in 2024.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="90"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results Indicator #8: The percentage of teachers who have attended training and demonstrate improved understanding of inclusive education, GBV, VAC and referral mechanisms</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-06-30" value="0" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="80">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">[Achieved] ECCE 96 percent (71 teachers out of total of 74 teachers), Primary 81 percent (121 teachers out of total of 150 teachers), and Secondary 88 percent (52 teachers out of total of 59 teachers) have been trained by early 2024.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="86.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results Indicator #6: Percent of new public buildings and dwellings complying with Building Code.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-06-30" value="0%" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-06-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
